            <ArticleTitle>Sudden ST elevation with angina-like pain in myocarditis. An uncommon course of a common disease: strategic role of cardiac magnetic resonance.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>264-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.2459/JCM.0b013e3283212920</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A case of a young man with myocarditis simulating acute coronary syndrome is reported. The possibility of vasospasm is discussed. The use of cardiac magnetic resonance imaging (MRI) is highlighted.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
